# Application plugins

Sources: `packages/web/src/shared/lib/plugins/types.ts`, `api.ts`, `registry.ts`, and `setup.ts` in that directory.

- Inspect the actual API and slot consumers; a declared slot or permission does not prove a working product integration.
- Keep plugin access through the explicit host API and minimum required permissions. Inject domain data from the app layer rather than importing entity stores into shared infrastructure.
- Preserve contribution/event teardown and release plugin-owned timers/subscriptions on deactivation.
- Registry permission checks and namespaced storage are API conventions, not an isolation sandbox for arbitrary JavaScript running in the same page.
- Do not expose credentials or load untrusted remote scripts as routine feature work. Verify the trust/deployment contract before extending dynamic loading.
- Add slots/events only when the requested feature requires them, not to every action bar by default.
